-- Business-day rolls counted from THE JOIN and THE ARMING (calendar library).
--
-- STATUS: proposed, not ruled (2026-10-24). specs/todo/ACT-TIME-GUARD-SPEC.md.
--
-- The companion of calendar-rollover.l4, written with the lifecycle nouns as
-- values instead of a day the act carries. That needs ruling B1
-- (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC.md §2.6), which is BUILT IN PART on
-- lang/lifecycle-values (2026-10-24) and NOT MERGED to unstable. This file is
-- kept apart so that the library and calendar-rollover.l4 do not depend on B1.
--
-- Dates, October and November 2026: Mon 26 Oct, Wed 28 Oct, Fri 30 Oct,
-- Sat 31 Oct, Mon 2 Nov, Tue 3 Nov, Thu 5 Nov.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT calendar

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Seller, Buyer, Landlord

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    notify
    pay
    serve HAS day IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Wed 21 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 21)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Mon 26 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 26)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Fri 30 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 30)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sat 31 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 31)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Mon 2 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 2)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Tue 3 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 3)


-- §1 Reading (b), counted from the notice itself. THE JOIN is the time the
-- notice was given (its AT stamp), so the notice carries no day of its own.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`pay within five days of notice, rolled` MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST notify WITHIN 10
    HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST pay WITHIN 0 OF (`next business day on or after` `weekdays only` (THE JOIN PLUS 5))

-- notice Mon 26 Oct: the fifth day, Sat 31 Oct, rolls to Mon 2 Nov
#TRACE `pay within five days of notice, rolled` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify AT `Mon 26 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Mon 2 Nov`

#TRACE `pay within five days of notice, rolled` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify AT `Mon 26 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Tue 3 Nov`


-- §2 (a) and (b) together, counted from the obligation's own arming: THE
-- ARMING on a top-level obligation is when it was entered.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`serve on a business day within ten days, rolled` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord MUST serve d PROVIDED `is a business day` `weekdays only` d
    WITHIN 0 OF (`next business day on or after` `weekdays only` (THE ARMING PLUS 10))

-- entered Wed 21 Oct: ten days end on Sat 31 Oct, rolled to Mon 2 Nov
#TRACE `serve on a business day within ten days, rolled` AT `Wed 21 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Sat 31 Oct` AT `Sat 31 Oct`
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`


-- §3 A TRAP, pinned. THE JOIN in a continuation's PROVIDED is the PREVIOUS
-- act, not the act being tested. The guard below reads as "the payment must
-- be made on a business day", and what it tests is the notice's day. Notice
-- on Fri 30 Oct (a business day), payment on Sat 31 Oct: the payment counts.
-- To guard the payment's own day, the payment has to carry it (as in
-- calendar-rollover.l4 §2); no noun names the act under test.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`pay on a business day, written wrongly` MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST notify WITHIN 10
    HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST pay PROVIDED `is a business day` `weekdays only` THE JOIN
          WITHIN 5

#TRACE `pay on a business day, written wrongly` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify AT `Fri 30 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Sat 31 Oct`
